// Register promotion -- SOURCE program.
//
// rmm-zoo property: rp (Global transformations / Register promotion).
// Source: Moiseenko, Podkopaev & Koznov, "A Survey of Programming Language
//         Memory Models" (2021), Tables 1-2 -- the Global transformations group;
//         Sevcik, "Safe Optimisations for Shared-Memory Concurrent Programs"
//         (PLDI 2011).
//
// Register promotion caches a shared location in a register across a region with
// no intervening synchronisation, so the loads inside the region read the
// register rather than memory and only the final value is written back. It is a
// GLOBAL transformation because its soundness depends on the whole region, not
// on an adjacent pair of accesses -- and it is the reason the zoo has rp as a
// column of its own. The zoo records rp = true for every model that has the cell
// (12 of them), but has no cell for MRD or sMRD.
//
// Here x is read back twice after being written; opt.lit replaces both reads by
// the promoted register value.
x := 0;
y := 0;
x := 1;
r1 := x;
x := 2;
r2 := x;
y := r1 + r2
